<h1>TCS Project — Work Plan Meeting Note</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Sukesh P (M24IM1007) &middot; Prep for 2:30 PM work-plan discussion &middot; 18 September 2026</p>
<p class="note">Goal for this meeting: extract exact scope, deliverable, timeline, and my responsibilities from Prof. Ajay — not to lock in a detailed plan from assumptions. Everything below marked "known" comes from the sepsis SERS biosensor work already done (Co-PIs: TCS); everything else is a question to ask.</p>

<h2>Objective (as understood so far — to be confirmed)</h2>
<p>Develop a SERS-based biosensor platform for label-free detection of sepsis biomarkers (NAM, LTA, LPS) as a step toward a point-of-care diagnostic. <strong>TCS's specific role/interest in this (hardware, software/AI, data infrastructure, productization?) is not yet defined — this is question #1 below.</strong></p>

<h2>Current Status</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Area</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
<tr><td>Requirement understanding</td><td class="status-progress">In progress</td><td>Overall biosensor goal is clear (NAM/LTA/LPS detection via Raman/SERS). TCS-specific requirement/scope not yet received.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Literature/background</td><td class="status-done">Completed (for current phase)</td><td>Targeted SERS literature review done for all three biomarkers, incl. direct benchmarks (Wu 2021, Yang 2022 for LPS) and substrate-fabrication literature (Kochylas 2021 and others for Ag/Si MACE).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Existing prototype/code</td><td class="status-pending">Not started</td><td>No hardware device or software prototype yet. Only lab-bench substrate fabrication + benchtop Raman measurement so far — no integrated system.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Dataset/data</td><td class="status-progress">Partial</td><td>Raw Raman spectra from 3 lab sessions (fabrication/R6G/NAM, instrument calibration, LTA attempt) plus DFT-computed reference spectra for all three biomarkers. No clinical or cultured-bacterial-isolate data yet.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hardware</td><td class="status-progress">Partial</td><td>Benchtop Raman spectrometer (785 nm) and substrate-fabrication setup (Si/Ag/HF) available. No dedicated/portable device hardware exists.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Software</td><td class="status-progress">Partial</td><td>Custom Python spectral preprocessing pipeline exists (smoothing, baseline correction, normalization). No ML/classification pipeline or application software yet.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Testing</td><td class="status-progress">In progress</td><td>Substrate SERS-activity validated (R6G control, strong signal). Biomarker detection attempted for NAM and LTA — both currently negative (see below). LPS SERS not yet attempted.</td></tr>
</table>

<p><strong>Completed:</strong> DFT + powder Raman reference spectra for NAM, LTA, LPS; substrate fabrication process established; SERS-activity of substrates confirmed (R6G).<br>
<strong>Ongoing:</strong> Biomarker SERS detection experiments (LPS next, then NAM optimization, then LTA repeat) — full protocol and timeline already drafted.<br>
<strong>Not started:</strong> Any hardware/software prototype, ML/AI classification, clinical-sample validation, point-of-care device work.</p>

<h2>Proposed Work Packages (draft — to revise after this meeting)</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Requirement analysis</strong> — capture TCS's exact problem statement and deliverable expectations</li>
<li><strong>System design</strong> — define what "the system" is (sensor only? sensor + software? sensor + device?), architecture accordingly</li>
<li><strong>Development</strong> — biomarker SERS detection (in progress, my current track) + any software/AI/hardware component TCS defines</li>
<li><strong>Integration</strong> — combine sensing, data pipeline, and any device/software component</li>
<li><strong>Testing</strong> — functional, performance, and validation testing per TCS's expected rigor level</li>
<li><strong>Documentation &amp; demo</strong> — technical documentation, prototype/demo, report</li>
</ol>

<h2>Proposed Milestones (rough — needs Prof. Ajay's timeline input)</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Milestone</th><th>Content</th></tr>
<tr><td>M1</td><td>Scope + requirements locked; architecture defined</td></tr>
<tr><td>M2</td><td>First confirmed biomarker SERS detection (LPS, per current experimental roadmap)</td></tr>
<tr><td>M3</td><td>Core module(s) developed/integrated per TCS scope</td></tr>
<tr><td>M4</td><td>Testing/validation complete; demo-ready prototype + documentation</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>My Possible Responsibilities (not yet confirmed — let Prof. Ajay define first)</h2>
<ul>
<li>SERS experimentation and biomarker detection (already my current track)</li>
<li>Python-based data analysis / spectral processing (already doing this)</li>
<li>AI/ML classification, if that becomes part of TCS's scope</li>
<li>Backend/API or data-pipeline work, if a software/data component is required</li>
<li>Domain/medical-technology input (sepsis biomarker rationale)</li>
</ul>

<h2>Resources Required (to flag, not finalize)</h2>
<ul>
<li>Chemicals/consumables for ongoing SERS experiments (separately tracked in lab procurement list)</li>
<li>Any TCS-provided data, specifications, hardware, or platform access — unknown until scope is defined</li>
<li>Compute/software resources if an AI/ML component is in scope</li>
</ul>

<h2>Questions for Prof. Ajay (priority order)</h2>
<div class="qbox">
<ol>
<li><strong>What is the exact TCS requirement/problem statement?</strong></li>
<li>What is the expected final deliverable — proof of concept, working prototype, or deployable system?</li>
<li>Is there an existing prototype/system we need to extend, or are we starting fresh?</li>
<li>What TCS-provided resources/data/specifications exist, if any?</li>
<li>What is the expected project duration and milestone schedule?</li>
<li>Who is the technical point of contact from TCS?</li>
<li>What technologies/platforms does TCS expect (specific software stack, hardware constraints, etc.)?</li>
<li>What testing/validation requirements does TCS expect?</li>
<li>What should be completed in the first 1&ndash;2 weeks?</li>
<li>How does this TCS work-plan relate to the ongoing SERS biomarker-detection experiments — is it the same deliverable track, or a separate/parallel one?</li>
</ol>
</div>

</div>
